{"uid":"b5fa11e5ffd57313","name":"test_a_kept_filing_emits_no_history_event","fullName":"tests.test_petitions#test_a_kept_filing_emits_no_history_event","historyId":"60d579e8a9e05aef89212501e0a7ce67","time":{"start":1791891139001,"stop":1791891139003,"duration":2},"description":"The no-op contract this module's other event emitters already\n    keep: a filing that resolves against an anchor stays open and costs\n    no history event. Task 013 (requirement E.5, #212) added a SECOND,\n    orthogonal event on this same call -- `PETITIONS_PATHS_READ_EVENT`,\n    recording which paths were read regardless of outcome -- so\n    `events.jsonl` is no longer empty on this path; the claim this test\n    actually makes (no *history* event) is asserted on that event type\n    specifically, exactly as `test_a_history_drop_emits_an_event_naming_\n    the_filing` above already asserts on its own type rather than on the\n    whole file.","descriptionHtml":"<p>The no-op contract this module's other event emitters already<br />\nkeep: a filing that resolves against an anchor stays open and costs<br />\nno history event. Task 013 (requirement E.5, #212) added a SECOND,<br />\northogonal event on this same call -- <code>PETITIONS_PATHS_READ_EVENT</code>,<br />\nrecording which paths were read regardless of outcome -- so<br />\n<code>events.jsonl</code> is no longer empty on this path; the claim this test<br />\nactually makes (no <em>history</em> event) is asserted on that event type<br />\nspecifically, exactly as <code>test_a_history_drop_emits_an_event_naming_ the_filing</code> above already asserts on its own type rather than on the<br />\nwhole file.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791891119391,"stop":1791891119391,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":fals